From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] feat: inject flavor nodeselectors and tolerations onto pods before ungating

When Kueue admits elastic workloads with zero initial replicas or reassigns flavors across slices, newly created pods bypass the initial job template injection cycle and lack the node selectors and tolerations required by their assigned ResourceFlavor. As a result, ungated pods can schedule onto incompatible cluster nodes or fail scheduling entirely.

Defer flavor node selectors and tolerations from elastic job pod templates to individual pods, recording the deferral on the Workload. In ElasticJobUngater, dynamically inject assigned flavor node selectors and tolerations onto gated pods before removing the scheduling gate, recycling any pods whose immutable specs conflict with updated flavor placement.
---
